    "body": "> Also no handling for `..` and such anywhere. Very strange.\n\nIs `..` a valid path attribute? [RFC6265bis](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-httpbis-rfc6265bis-20#section-5.6.4) would have us ignore that value and use the default path. In Chrome, the Cookie Store API rejects a cookie whose `path`  option does not start with `/` (with the exception of empty string).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
