    "created_at": "2025-09-12T15:56:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-12T15:56:00Z",
    "body": "> Where does it handle it?\n\nCould have been more clear there. What I meant is the Cookie Store API spec handles paths with those characters by passing them along to the cookie storage model. The character `.` is not reserved in URL paths so it could be a valid path.\n\nThe resolving to the parent path seems to be due to our implementation. I would expect the behavior to match document.cookie's Path attribute, but that does not seem to be happening. I have filed [a bug against Chromium](https://crbug.com/444671413) to investigate this issue with our implementation.\n\nRegardless of Chrome-specific quirks, I think the spec is still handling `..` correctly, i.e. deferring to RFC6265bis to handle the cookie path string containing `..`.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
